{
 "ios-navigation|Sidebars": {
  "summary": "A Plenix sidebar on iOS is the system sidebar list (a List with the sidebar style in a NavigationSplitView, or a UICollectionView sidebar layout), kept native in behavior: it shows by default, hides with the usual gesture or command, folds disclosure groups, floats over rich content on iPad, and supports Dynamic Type, VoiceOver and the keyboard. Plenix changes the look to match the Web NavPane and NavList: 44-point rows with a 6-point rounded selection in the Plenix selected colors, DM Sans row titles at the body text role, muted section headers at the eyebrow role, and muted symbols with color only when it carries meaning.",
